plying that fool''s trade in Paris. We sat down at a table; the Tsarist ordered wine, and Valeria, after applying a wet napkin to […]","pages":[21],"terms":["Paris"],"category":"action","context":false,"rationale":"La rivelazione di Valeria, il taxi e il colloquio al caffè sono azioni ambientate a Parigi, non informazioni anagrafiche.","reference_id":"9:core:paris"},{"section":9,"original_section":"1.8","place_id":"italy","quote":"[…] also have such coruscating trifles as A vagabond in Italy by Percy Elphinstone, author of Venice Revisited, Boston, 1868, and […]","pages":[25],"terms":["Italy"],"category":"mentioned","context":false,"reference_id":"9:core:italy"},{"section":9,"original_section":"1.8","place_id":"new-york","quote":"[…] I informed her we were shortly to sail for New York, she looked distressed and bewildered. […]","pages":[21],"terms":["New York"],"category":"mentioned","context":false,"reference_id":"9:core:new-york"},{"section":9,"original_section":"1.8","place_id":"california","quote":"[…] died in childbirth around 1945; the couple had somehow got over to California and had been used there, for an excellent salary, in a year-long […] constant position on all fours. My informant, a doctor, swore he had seen with his own eyes obese Valechka […]","pages":[24],"terms":["California"],"category":"action","context":false,"rationale":"Il medico racconta ciò che ha visto nell’esperimento californiano. È una scena nel racconto intercalato, non un viaggio di Humbert.","reference_id":"9:core:california"},{"section":9,"original_section":"1.8","place_id":"pasadena","quote":"[…] A man from Pasadena told me one day that Mrs. […]","pages":[24],"terms":["Pasadena"],"category":"mentioned","context":false,"reference_id":"9:core:pasadena"},{"section":9,"original_section":"1.8","place_id":"venice","quote":"[…] A vagabond in Italy by Percy Elphinstone, author of Venice Revisited, Boston, 1868, and a comparatively recent (1946) Who''s Who […]","pages":[25],"terms":["Venice"],"category":"mentioned","context":false,"reference_id":"9:core:venice"},{"section":9,"original_section":"1.8","place_id":"boston","quote":"[…] in Italy by Percy Elphinstone, author of Venice Revisited, Boston, 1868, and a comparatively recent (1946) Who''s Who in the […]","pages":[25],"terms":["Boston"],"category":"mentioned","context":false,"reference_id":"9:core:boston"},{"section":9,"original_section":"1.8","place_id":"ocean-city","quote":"[…] Born in Ocean City, N.J., 1911. […]","pages":[25],"terms":["Ocean City"],"category":"mentioned","context":false,"reference_id":"9:core:ocean-city"},{"section":9,"original_section":"1.8","place_id":"columbia-university","quote":"[…] Educated at Columbia University. […]","pages":[25],"terms":["Columbia University"],"category":"mentioned","context":false,"reference_id":"9:core:columbia-university"},{"section":9,"original_section":"1.8","place_id":"dayton","quote":"[…] Born in 1882, in Dayton, Ohio. […]","pages":[25],"terms":["Dayton"],"category":"mentioned","context":false,"reference_id":"9:core:dayton"},{"section":9,"original_section":"1.8","place_id":"ottawa","quote":"[…] First played in Ottawa in 1900. […]","pages":[25],"terms":["Ottawa"],"category":"mentioned","context":false,"reference_id":"9:core:ottawa"},{"section":9,"original_section":"1.8","place_id":"ohio","quote":"[…] Born in 1882, in Dayton, Ohio. […]","pages":[25],"terms":["Ohio"],"category":"mentioned","context":false,"reference_id":"9:core:ohio"},{"section":9,"original_section":"1.8","place_id":"America","quote":"[…] her so listless, despite my patiently describing to her America, the country of rosy children and great trees, where life […]","pages":[21],"terms":["America"],"category":"mentioned","context":false,"ordinal":0,"name":"America"},{"section":9,"original_section":"1.8","place_id":"Lundy","quote":"[…] Born in Lundy, Mass., 1922. […]","pages":[25],"terms":["Lundy"],"category":"mentioned","context":false,"ordinal":1,"name":"Lundy"},{"section":9,"original_section":"1.8","place_id":"Derby","quote":"[…] Received stage training at Elsinore Playhouse, Derby, N.Y. […]","pages":[25],"terms":["Derby"],"category":"mentioned","context":false,"ordinal":2,"name":"Derby"},{"section":10,"original_section":"1.9","place_id":"new-york","quote":"[…] In New York I eagerly accepted the soft job fate offered me: it […]","pages":[25],"terms":["New York"],"category":"mentioned","context":false,"reference_id":"10:core:new-york"},{"section":10,"original_section":"1.9","place_id":"portugal","quote":"[…] when, after a winter of ennui and pneumonia in Portugal, I at last reached the States. […]","pages":[25],"terms":["Portugal"],"category":"mentioned","context":false,"reference_id":"10:core:portugal"},{"section":10,"original_section":"1.9","place_id":"central-park","quote":"[…] a glimpse of nymphets (alas, always remote) playing in Central Park, and how repulsed I was by the glitter of deodorized […]","pages":[26],"terms":["Central Park"],"category":"mentioned","context":false,"reference_id":"10:core:central-park"},{"section":10,"original_section":"1.9","place_id":"victoria-island","quote":"[…] expedition; which, in conclusion, was not really concerned with Victoria Island copper or anything like that, as I learned later from […]","pages":[27],"terms":["Victoria Island"],"category":"mentioned","context":false,"reference_id":"10:core:victoria-island"},{"section":10,"original_section":"1.9","place_id":"regional-arctic-canada","quote":"[…] was about to lead an expedition into arctic Canada. […] whistling gale; seated on a boulder under a completely translucent sky (through which, however, nothing of importance showed), […]","pages":[26,27],"terms":["arctic Canada"],"category":"action","context":false,"rationale":"Il narratore descrive se stesso seduto sul masso durante la spedizione. Prince of Wales e Victoria non identificano il campo: il primo è un’ipotesi sullo scopo, il secondo è negato.","region_index":17},{"section":10,"original_section":